      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Let's start by expanding each of the products separately. For $(2x - 5)(x + 7)$, we use the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n(2x - 5)(x + 7) = 2x \\cdot x + 2x \\cdot 7 - 5 \\cdot x - 5 \\cdot 7 = 2x^2 + 14x - 5x - 35 = 2x^2 + 9x - 35\n\\]\n\nFor $(x + 5)(2x - 1)$, we also use the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n(x + 5)(2x - 1) = x \\cdot 2x + x \\cdot (-1) + 5 \\cdot 2x + 5 \\cdot (-1) = 2x^2 - x + 10x - 5 = 2x^2 + 9x - 5\n\\]\n\nNow we substitute these expanded forms back into the original expression:\n\n\\[\n(2x - 5)(x + 7) - (x + 5)(2x - 1) = (2x^2 + 9x - 35) - (2x^2 + 9x - 5)\n\\]\n\nNext, we distribute the negative sign through the second set of parentheses:\n\n\\[\n2x^2 + 9x - 35 - 2x^2 - 9x + 5\n\\]\n\nNow we combine like terms. The $2x^2$ and $-2x^2$ terms cancel each other out, as do the $9x$ and $-9x$ terms:\n\n\\[\n2x^2 - 2x^2 + 9x - 9x - 35 + 5 = 0 + 0 - 30 = -30\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the simplified form of the expression is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-30}\n\\]",
